  "unmapped_findings": [
    "Baseline for comparison (parent as-hot-rolled condition, not this solution-treated sample): the same Fe-30Mn-9Al-2.7Si-0.9C steel (0.023% P, 50 µm average grain size) had room-temperature CVN breaking energies of 23 J (L-T orientation) and 22 J (T-L orientation), with mainly transgranular cleavage-type fracture; the cleavage facets displayed slip traces at roughly 60° angles from one another, indicating fracture by decohesion of active slip planes.",
    "The large CVN energy difference between the hot-rolled and solution-treated conditions is related to short-range ordering (SRO) and precipitation of j-carbide, because the hot-rolled material was slow cooled after deformation."
  ]
